WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.031 --> 00:00:02.751
needs a new generation at the table to fix things.

00:00:05.176 --> 00:00:08.676
And that New Hampshire needs independent leadership to stand up and

00:00:08.676 --> 00:00:09.676
get stuff done.

00:00:12.616 --> 00:00:15.496
You know, throughout, throughout this campaign, you invited me into

00:00:15.496 --> 00:00:20.096
your homes, your community centers, and your small businesses. You

00:00:20.096 --> 00:00:23.736
shared with me your challenges, your fears, and your hopes for the

00:00:23.736 --> 00:00:24.316
future.

00:00:24.856 --> 00:00:29.216
And tonight I am honored beyond words to have earned your votes to

00:00:29.216 --> 00:00:31.436
fight for you in the United States Senate.

00:00:36.856 --> 00:00:41.016
A few minutes ago I just got a very gracious call from John Sununu.

00:00:41.576 --> 00:00:45.136
He wished us, he wished us and our team well, and I wish the same

00:00:45.136 --> 00:00:50.216
for him and his family, and I think we all owe John Sununu a big

00:00:50.216 --> 00:00:53.626
debt of gratitude for his public service for the people of New Hampshire.

00:00:56.536 --> 00:00:56.856
So

00:00:56.856 --> 00:00:57.116
tonight

00:00:57.736 --> 00:01:00.776
Whether you're a Republican, an Independent, or a Democrat, tonight's

00:01:00.776 --> 00:01:05.286
victory is for you because this is a victory for Team New Hampshire

00:01:05.286 --> 00:01:08.876
over the broken status quo that is hurting all of us just the same.

00:01:12.936 --> 00:01:14.256
Tonight's results.

00:01:14.696 --> 00:01:17.766
Tonight's results are a wake-up call for corporate special interests

00:01:17.766 --> 00:01:21.096
and billionaires who have been rigging the economy for the cowards

00:01:21.096 --> 00:01:25.096
in Congress who have enabled healthcare cuts, tariffs, and war, and

00:01:25.096 --> 00:01:28.776
for the incompetent president who can't even be bothered to care

00:01:28.776 --> 00:01:32.486
how people are being hurt. So tonight, voters in New Hampshire and

00:01:32.486 --> 00:01:36.416
all across the country simply have had enough and are demanding a

00:01:36.416 --> 00:01:40.176
change in direction, and I am ready to fight with everything I've

00:01:40.176 --> 00:01:42.596
got to deliver the change that we need.

00:01:47.186 --> 00:01:47.986
So

00:01:48.956 --> 00:01:51.876
Here in New Hampshire, here in New Hampshire, we are clear-eyed about

00:01:51.876 --> 00:01:55.036
the scale of the challenges that we face and the hard work that it

00:01:55.036 --> 00:01:57.796
will take to move forward, whether it's building the housing New

00:01:57.796 --> 00:02:01.996
Hampshire needs, expanding access to healthcare and childcare, saving

00:02:01.996 --> 00:02:05.876
Social Security, protecting our planet, restoring reproductive freedom,

00:02:05.956 --> 00:02:09.916
rooting out corruption, or holding this administration accountable,

00:02:09.996 --> 00:02:12.016
we don't have a moment to waste, do we?

00:02:14.856 --> 00:02:18.126
But there will of course be moments that test our resolve. There

00:02:18.126 --> 00:02:21.596
will be times when we hit roadblocks and get frustrated with the

00:02:21.596 --> 00:02:26.096
pace of progress, but we can never give up, and we must be committed

00:02:26.096 --> 00:02:30.216
to renewing the purpose of American democracy and working with persistence

00:02:30.216 --> 00:02:34.406
and urgency each and every day. I'll be honored to stand with the

00:02:34.406 --> 00:02:37.856
people of New Hampshire shoulder to shoulder in that work, and I'll

00:02:37.856 --> 00:02:41.276
work with anyone who can deliver a better life for Granite Staters,

00:02:41.416 --> 00:02:44.776
and I'll stand up to anyone who will take us back, you know.

00:02:44.856 --> 00:02:47.896
Across this state, Granite Staters are showing the fighting spirit,

00:02:48.176 --> 00:02:51.576
the resilience, and the determination that we're known for protesting

00:02:51.576 --> 00:02:55.256
against the reckless policies coming out of Washington, organizing

00:02:55.256 --> 00:02:58.296
against corporate landlords buying up homes and jacking up the rent,

00:02:58.696 --> 00:03:03.236
opposing big data centers that harm our communities and our well-being

00:03:03.576 --> 00:03:06.736
and stopping an ICE detention center from being built in the state

00:03:06.736 --> 00:03:07.716
of New Hampshire.

00:03:13.416 --> 00:03:17.996
We're also a state, we're also a state that shows compassion, mobilizing

00:03:17.996 --> 00:03:20.936
for our friends and neighbors, for veterans, for folks struggling

00:03:20.936 --> 00:03:24.976
with addiction or families who are in need of food or shelter. That's

00:03:24.976 --> 00:03:28.206
how we do things in the state of New Hampshire. We step up, we roll

00:03:28.206 --> 00:03:31.366
up our sleeves, and we make it happen. And that's the spirit I'll

00:03:31.366 --> 00:03:34.136
bring to my work in the United States Senate for all of you.

00:03:38.306 --> 00:03:41.746
So tonight, tonight we don't celebrate a victory for any one political

00:03:41.746 --> 00:03:45.886
party. We celebrate a victory for anyone, left, right, or center,

00:03:46.106 --> 00:03:49.446
struggling with the skyrocketing cost of living from gas to groceries

00:03:49.446 --> 00:03:53.466
to housing. Anyone who's sick of the tariffs, the endless war, the

00:03:53.466 --> 00:03:57.326
tax breaks for big corporations paid for by cuts to your healthcare.

00:03:57.666 --> 00:04:00.766
Anyone who's fed up with the most corrupt president in our history

00:04:00.906 --> 00:04:04.546
who has failed in his way of governing, and anyone who knows that

00:04:04.546 --> 00:04:08.226
we can do so much better if we work together. So we know this was.

00:04:08.306 --> 00:04:12.106
A hard fought victory tonight. It was made even harder by the tens

00:04:12.106 --> 00:04:14.866
and tens of millions of dollars that poured into New Hampshire from

00:04:14.866 --> 00:04:18.186
Donald Trump, Elon Musk, and corporate special interests who are

00:04:18.186 --> 00:04:19.086
just fine.

00:04:20.296 --> 00:04:23.696
Who are just fine with the way things are going right now. They threw

00:04:23.696 --> 00:04:27.056
money, attack ads, and outright lies at us every day for months.

00:04:27.456 --> 00:04:29.116
But we beat him anyway, didn't we?

00:04:33.656 --> 00:04:37.966
We were never, we were never the big money campaign. We're the people

00:04:37.966 --> 00:04:42.416
powered campaign, a campaign of 200,000 individual donors and not

00:04:42.416 --> 00:04:44.326
a dime from corporate PACs.

00:04:45.656 --> 00:04:49.376
And we showed what happens when we stick together, stand up for what's

00:04:49.376 --> 00:04:52.436
right, and never lose hope even when the odds are long.

00:04:52.776 --> 00:04:57.656
It was 579 days ago that we gathered in this very room, a place where

00:04:57.656 --> 00:05:00.936
we've celebrated many victories with more to come tonight.

00:05:01.536 --> 00:05:05.226
And a place that has taught me everything about serving the community

00:05:05.226 --> 00:05:08.616
that I know and love that has given me so many opportunities in my

00:05:08.616 --> 00:05:12.256
life. Nearly 20 months ago, I said I knew we were living in deeply

00:05:12.256 --> 00:05:14.766
uncertain times, but I knew something else

00:05:15.336 --> 00:05:19.216
that granted staters don't flinch. We don't give in. We stand up

00:05:19.216 --> 00:05:22.276
and fight, and that's exactly what we did in this campaign.

00:05:24.456 --> 00:05:27.976
The fight we started in this room and took to every corner of New

00:05:27.976 --> 00:05:32.336
Hampshire is now headed to Washington to get our state and our country

00:05:32.336 --> 00:05:34.096
on the right track for the future.

00:05:36.456 --> 00:05:36.696
And

00:05:36.696 --> 00:05:37.376
so

00:05:38.856 --> 00:05:42.676
And so I'll end tonight by saying this, I am so grateful for everyone

00:05:42.676 --> 00:05:46.496
in this room and beyond who made this win possible. I want to thank

00:05:46.496 --> 00:05:50.056
my extended family who has always shown up for me each and every

00:05:50.056 --> 00:05:54.856
day, to my amazing parents who have set the best example of public

00:05:54.856 --> 00:05:55.556
service.

00:05:56.456 --> 00:05:59.896
And hard work and giving back to the community and unconditional

00:05:59.896 --> 00:06:00.186
love.

00:06:01.756 --> 00:06:04.456
I want to thank the guy next to me, my amazing husband Van.

00:06:13.496 --> 00:06:14.196
How about it?

00:06:25.036 --> 00:06:27.496
Alright, the wrong person was on the ballot apparently.

00:06:28.936 --> 00:06:32.086
But he's always been by my side, and look, tonight, win, lose or

00:06:32.086 --> 00:06:35.756
draw, I'm the luckiest guy because I'm married to a man that I love.

00:06:40.376 --> 00:06:40.496
And

00:06:40.496 --> 00:06:41.156
despite

00:06:42.216 --> 00:06:46.416
All the negative attacks and the lies. It's nice to know that love

00:06:46.416 --> 00:06:47.716
and truth prevailed tonight.

00:06:50.856 --> 00:06:54.216
I want to thank my amazing campaign staff led by our campaign manager

00:06:54.216 --> 00:06:55.256
Rachel Petrie.

00:06:58.796 --> 00:07:02.156
who ran the most effective campaign our state has seen.

00:07:04.376 --> 00:07:07.496
I want to thank Beth Cunn and all the organizers at Organizing for

00:07:07.496 --> 00:07:08.396
New Hampshire.

00:07:08.796 --> 00:07:10.776
For the work you did to get out the vote.

00:07:12.776 --> 00:07:16.326
You worked hard over the past year communicating with voters on the

00:07:16.326 --> 00:07:19.576
issues that matter and you've got it done. I want to thank our I

00:07:19.576 --> 00:07:23.046
thank our friends in organized labor as well who stood shoulder to

00:07:23.046 --> 00:07:24.626
shoulder with us in this campaign.

00:07:25.116 --> 00:07:28.996
And I can't wait to continuing to work with all of you to build a

00:07:28.996 --> 00:07:32.036
fairer future for everyone who calls New Hampshire home. Thank you

00:07:32.036 --> 00:07:35.586
to all the volunteers, the folks who chipped in, who knocked on doors,

00:07:35.636 --> 00:07:39.836
who made phone calls, who got voters' rides to the polls who talk

00:07:39.836 --> 00:07:42.676
to your friends and neighbors about the stakes. I wouldn't be standing

00:07:42.676 --> 00:07:46.166
before you giving this speech tonight if it weren't for the thousands

00:07:46.166 --> 00:07:48.916
of folks who have stepped up for this campaign. Thanks for being

00:07:48.916 --> 00:07:49.776
a part of this.

00:07:52.396 --> 00:07:55.226
And I want to thank the team in my congressional office too, led

00:07:55.226 --> 00:07:57.236
by Stephen Carlson and Carrie Thurman.

00:08:02.556 --> 00:08:03.096
Dave.

00:08:04.076 --> 00:08:07.316
They've spent the past 8 years stepping up for granted staters and

00:08:07.316 --> 00:08:10.556
meeting the needs of our constituents and the entire district, and

00:08:10.556 --> 00:08:13.576
I just salute them for all their hard work on behalf of New Hampshire.

00:08:16.376 --> 00:08:19.536
I want to thank my friend of the New Hampshire delegation, the amazing

00:08:19.536 --> 00:08:22.036
Senator Maggie Hassan, for joining us here tonight.

00:08:24.536 --> 00:08:27.496
It's going to be an honor to be with her as part of the team in the

00:08:27.496 --> 00:08:30.256
United States Senate working closely together for the people of this

00:08:30.256 --> 00:08:30.716
state.

00:08:31.416 --> 00:08:34.336
And I want to send my best wishes to my friend Maggie Goodlander

00:08:34.336 --> 00:08:35.396
on her victory tonight.

00:08:38.776 --> 00:08:41.896
And my friend, who I think you'll be hearing from shortly, Stephanie

00:08:41.896 --> 00:08:42.586
Shaheen.

00:08:47.436 --> 00:08:51.516
Look, before I close, I just want to recognize someone who is important

00:08:51.516 --> 00:08:55.316
to all of us here in this room, and who's made an immeasurable difference

00:08:55.316 --> 00:08:58.156
for the people of New Hampshire throughout her time in public service,

00:08:58.396 --> 00:09:00.306
and that's the great Senator Jeanne Shaheen.

00:09:15.256 --> 00:09:19.326
Senator Shaheen has set the standard we should all strive for in

00:09:19.326 --> 00:09:22.256
public service, and I couldn't be more grateful to call her a colleague

00:09:22.256 --> 00:09:25.456
and a friend. We know that New Hampshire is a better place because

00:09:25.456 --> 00:09:29.336
of the work she's done throughout her career and her impact on education,

00:09:29.446 --> 00:09:32.816
on healthcare, on the environment, the economy, and so many other

00:09:32.816 --> 00:09:37.086
crucial issues will stand the test of time. So know this no one will

00:09:37.086 --> 00:09:40.406
ever fill her shoes, but we all have got to carry on her good work,

00:09:40.496 --> 00:09:40.956
don't we?

00:09:43.256 --> 00:09:44.316
So tonight we celebrate.

00:09:45.496 --> 00:09:48.096
And as we celebrate, let's think about the brighter future that we

00:09:48.096 --> 00:09:51.976
can all build together. Let's remember what is possible when we join

00:09:51.976 --> 00:09:55.456
with common purpose and fight for a fairer, freer New Hampshire.

00:09:56.006 --> 00:09:59.816
Today, you all did your part. We all did our part to put our state

00:09:59.816 --> 00:10:03.136
and our country on a better path, and tomorrow we've got to get to

00:10:03.136 --> 00:10:06.136
work to fight for what's right and deliver the solutions that are

00:10:06.136 --> 00:10:08.136
desperately needed, so.

00:10:08.536 --> 00:10:13.336
My my words to you tonight are thank you and let's keep going. Let's

00:10:13.336 --> 00:10:14.036
keep going.

00:10:15.656 --> 00:10:18.416
Let's keep going and fighting and working for the people of this

00:10:18.416 --> 00:10:21.516
great state. Thank you all for being here tonight. I really appreciate

00:10:21.516 --> 00:10:22.976
it. Thanks for standing with us.

